    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3275" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăquensis</span></b> , e, adj.
		Aquae, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Aquœ.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> To Aquae
			Taurīnae: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aquenses cognomine Taurini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 8, § 52</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> To
			Aquae Aureliae: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">CIVITAS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 928</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">949</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> To Aquae in Aquitania, now <i>Bagnères</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">VICANI,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 204</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b> To
			Aquae Helveticae, now <i>Wettingen</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 457</span></i>.</div>
